        }
      ],
      "message": "interfaces: fix findAncestorByHash returning true for unknown block\n\nWhen the block argument cannot be resolved via LookupBlockIndex (i.e. block is nullptr), findAncestorByHash previously left ancestor untouched, incorrectly returning true if ancestor was valid.\n\nFix this by ensuring ancestor is set to nullptr if either block or ancestor is null, or if block does not descend from ancestor. Add unit test assertions covering unknown block, unknown ancestor, both unknown, and height preservation.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Yudistira Putra",
